  {
    "episode_id": 83164,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83164.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Well, there's no yes or no answer. It's a no. You know, biological boys should not participate in sports against girls. I mean, bottom line, I've worked in sports all my life. One of the few things and best things that's ever happened here in Washington, D.C. was in 1972 when they passed Title IX. and made it equal for girls and boys in sports in terms of funding facilities, coaches, and look at the growth of women's sports. It's been unbelievable. But now, after 50 years, this administration wants to tear up Tylenine up. They don't believe in genders. They don't believe in moral values. They're trying to transition little kids, let them transition without telling their parents. This group has absolutely lost their mind. They're taking parents out of the equation of raising their kids. They won't government to raise their kids. And that's not going to happen on my watch. You know, I'm going to fight it. You got a lot of other people are going to fight it. I cannot believe that there's one Democrat, Senator or Congressman. that can look you and I and tell you that they're for this. They can't be because they've got daughters, they've got granddaughters. And you'd look for fairness in life. In this country, that's what we're about. We're about trust and fairness. Well, there's no fairness or trust in anything it has to do with transitioning biological boys to compete against girls. It's wrong. It's unfair and it's unsafe.",
